itle when ambiguous and reject an existing exact normalized title.\n2. Ask `/api/shelf-search?q=<title>&cat=<key>&mode=web`; take its **first web-image result**. This route uses Google Custom Search first and its built-in web fallback only when Google credentials are unavailable; never switch to the category auto-search/media results.\n3. POST that URL to `/api/shelf-img`; require `{ok:true,url}` (a commit-pinned jsDelivr URL).\n4. Read `shelf/<key>.json`, append `{id,name,score,status,tags:[],extra:{},image:{kind:'url',ref:url},notes:null}`, then save with the current SHA. On conflict, reread, dedupe, and retry up to 5 times.\n5. Re-read the live manifest and confirm the exact item and pinned image URL. For 100+ cards or a repair/migration, stop and apply `zenray-git-bulk-safety`.\n\nNever commit source code changes or store external poster URLs directly. Report title, category, status, score, and the immutable poster URL.\n\n\nARGUMENTS: The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt Songs of the Past\n\nLofsöng\n\n*Tides of Annihilation\nPetit Planet\n\ndans backlog category /shelf"}]},"isMeta":true,"turnCompanion":true,"uuid":"f0b3746a-e3a8-432a-96a7-85aad07d8f04","timestamp":"2026-08-29T19:27:01.391Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Downloads","sessionId":"b2e39d6e-ef3c-4f45-b5cb-db4db77ba16c","version":"2.1.247","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
